tp Event in "modules/process/event/protocol/event.kh"

// EventListener Usually implement on some kind of services that:
// - Carry log event to desire node and show on screen e.g. in control room of the organization
// - Notify to related person about critical log that must check as soon as possible by pager, sms, email, web notification, user GUI app, ...
// - Local GUI application to notify the developers in `log.CNF_DevelopingMode`
tp EventListener ab

// Synchrony, capture, once, passive, and an abort signal are not members here: each is a property of
// one registration rather than of a listener. What this protocol requires of the two parties instead,
// and where the answer to each of the five is stated:
// `modules/process/event/event.md` -> Why capture, once, passive, and synchrony are not members.
// What that document defers to a dispatch mechanism's own contract — whether a dispatch waits for its
// handlers, and the order a target visits its listeners in — is open state, not an answer:
// `modules/process/event/event.handoff.md` -> Open Questions.
tp EventHandler mt (self EventListener) (event Event) ()
